{"chunk_id": "b7b94be86cb5", "text": "Kumbhakarna marches out of Lanka to face Rama\u2019s monkey army and wades into battle with terrifying strength. The monkeys swarm him with trees, stones, and claws, but he laughs off the assault and even devours some of them. Sugriva attacks but is seized until Lakshmana intervenes, striking Kumbhakarna with powerful arrows. In a dramatic exchange, Lakshmana cuts off the giant\u2019s arms, which miraculously multiply, forcing an even greater display of skill. Finally Lakshmana uses a Brahma weapon to slay the monstrous warrior, causing the Rakshasa troops to panic. Other Rakshasas, including Vajravega and Promathin, attempt retaliation but are killed by Hanuman and Nala. The section ends with Ravana, enraged by these losses, sending his formidable son Indrajit to challenge Lakshmana to a decisive duel.\nKumbhakarna battles the monkey army but is slain by Lakshmana, after which Indrajit is sent by Ravana to confront Rama\u2019s forces.\nThemes: heroic combat, monkey army vs rakshasas, Lakshmana's prowess, fall of Kumbhakarna, escalation of war", "vector": [-0.0002565746253821999, -0.02300514467060566, -0.00043327026651240885, 0.01652783900499344, -0.01169662456959486, 0.02102448046207428, -0.016688432544469833, -0.013228962197899818, -0.029174646362662315, -0.014788066036999226, 0.009294399991631508, 0.004128613974899054, 0.01211149338632822, -0.0013608700828626752, -0.00017146796744782478, 0.003954636864364147, 0.03886384144425392, -0.013837882317602634, 0.025534506887197495, -0.02351369336247444, -0.0056776804849505424, -0.004580285865813494, -0.003964673727750778, -0.0004165416758041829, -0.03412630781531334, 0.014868363738059998, 0.02590922638773918, -0.03562518581748009, 0.012071344070136547, -0.012312236241996288, -0.014426728710532188, -0.021693624556064606, -0.00614273501560092, 0.0035263849422335625, -0.01895013637840748, -0.011890675872564316, -0.007808901835232973, -0.005055377259850502, 0.022576894611120224, -0.00265